From 12041ce250c738edfe6fc9c13b9e62ae8ea865a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 22:21:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 182/219] fix: the RT status lines reach the HUD and the log
 again

r_DisplayInfo 2 printed neither "RT pools:" nor "RT BVH:" even with a freshly
voxelized level, because by the time the user looked at the HUD
e_svoTI_RT_Active was already back to 0.

C3DEngine::UpdateTISettings assigned all five e_svoTI_RT_* cvars from the
level's TimeOfDay "TI advanced" params. Those five fields are never
serialized - their SerializeSvoTi lines in TimeOfDayConstants.cpp are
commented out ("Early version of RT is excluded from UI until we integrate
proper version from Neon Noir branch") - so rtActive is always the
constructor default false. Every ConstantsChanged() (level load, preset
load, any edit in the Environment Editor) therefore silently switched
triangle RT off. The write goes straight into the CVars struct member, not
through ICVar::Set, so nothing is logged and no OnChange fires.

The level params now apply only when the level actually asks for RT
(tiAdv.rtActive), which preserves stock behaviour for the four legacy cvars
whenever the switch is on and leaves the console in charge otherwise.

Also in this change:

- CSvoManager::OnDisplayInfo passed the status string as a printf FORMAT
  string. The pool line contains a literal '%' ("= 3.2%"), which makes an
  invalid conversion specifier and costs the whole line. It is passed as
  "%s" data now.
- Both RT lines test the cvar BEFORE slotId++, like the VoxSeg line, so a
  suppressed line does not consume a slot and silence later lines.
- CSvoEnv::m_rtStats was never initialised, so the BVH line printed heap
  garbage until the first build. RTCachePoolDims resets it.
- New CSvoEnv::RTFormatPoolLine / RTFormatBvhLine hold the two lines once;
  RTLogStatsWhenReady prints them to the log as "SVO RT: ..." once per
  completed voxelization pass, so the numbers are reachable even when the
  HUD is not.
- CSvoEnv::RTCountUvScaleMismatch: known gap 7.2 (one atlas UV scale per
  material) now counts offending materials, warns once per level naming the
  material, and reports the count as "texScale N" in the BVH line.
- New cvar e_svoTI_RT_LightGridDim (16), mirrored by the renderer in 2A.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SCUvWGLCsqzm3VNMzp4uiS
